  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "btle: Fix format truncation",
  "description": "The calculation of the longest possible string in one place\nomitted the underscore and always truncated the last digit.\nMake the calculation explicit to minimize issues. (On C23 this\ncould be a constexpr, but the compiler should still be able to\noptimize this.)\n\nFixes warning when -Werror=format-truncation is enabled on gcc:\n```c\npacket-btle.c:4402:65: error: ‘snprintf’ output truncated before the last format character [-Werror=format-truncation=]\n 4402 |             snprintf(str_addr_src, str_addr_len, \"Central_0x%08x\", broadcastiso_connection_info->access_address);\n      |                                                                 ^\npacket-btle.c:4402:13: note: ‘snprintf’ output 19 bytes into a destination of size 18\n 4402 |             snprintf(str_addr_src, str_addr_len, \"Central_0x%08x\", broadcastiso_connection_info->access_address);\n      |             ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n```\n\nMany of the other format truncation errors that gcc produces are\npathological cases (very long variable strings, or ints that should\nnot be negative being negative) but this one is always wrong.\n\nPing #19995",
  "state": "merged",
